# Clones created by benchmark/run.mjs (never committed).
work/

# Scratch space used by --mock (generated mock toolkit runner, mock target tree).
# Also ignored globally by the root .gitignore (temp/ and tmp/), declared here
# explicitly so the intent is visible next to the harness that writes it.
tmp/

# Local-only target list with the real repo URLs. The tracked repos.json is the
# label list (target-N aliases, empty urls); the label -> repo mapping is
# published in benchmark/targets.json. This file is never committed.
repos.local.json

# Raw per-module agent transcripts from Arm C orchestrated runs (lote 2).
# ~3.7 MB of LLM output; the graded artifacts (assessment.json, scores.json,
# SUMMARY.md) and input digests ARE committed. Excluded transcripts are listed
# with sha256 in results-lote2-deepseek/MODULES-EXCLUDED.sha256 so the evidence
# is hash-verifiable without shipping the bulk.
results-lote2-deepseek/*/orchestrated/modules/

# Per-repo report dumps from the 2026-10-07 detect sweep (19 repos x findings.json,
# report.md, prompts.md): 57 files, ~4.35 MB of generated output. The summary evidence
# (SWEEP.md, sweep.json, run-log.json), the timeout diagnostics (diag/) and every repo's
# invocation record (runs/<repo>/run.cmd, stdout.txt, stderr.txt, exit.txt) ARE
# committed, so each figure in SWEEP.md stays backed by a committed artifact without
# shipping 4.35 MB of duplicated dumps. Same reasoning as the excluded modules above.
detect-sweep-2026-10-07/runs/*/findings.json
detect-sweep-2026-10-07/runs/*/report.md
detect-sweep-2026-10-07/runs/*/prompts.md

# The per-rule / per-file timeout bisection logs ARE the diagnostic evidence SWEEP.md
# points at (diag/<repo>/diag.log names code-many-params-10 as the hang; diag/file/...
# names the single triggering file). The root "*.log" rule would swallow them, so they
# are re-included explicitly. ~7 KB total.
!detect-sweep-2026-10-07/diag/**/*.log
